---
// Prerendered at build time so the same page is served from S3/CloudFront and the container.
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Mysterium"
	description="Who writes this journal and how the site is built."
	pubDate={new Date('September 14 2026')}
	key="F#"
>
	<p>
		<strong>Mysterium</strong> is a piano journal about Alexander Scriabin (1872–1915), named after
		the vast multimedia work he planned but never finished. I write about the pieces on my piano
		stand, the ideas behind them, and Scriabin's unusual habit of hearing music in colour.
	</p>

	<h2>How it is built</h2>
	<p>
		The site is an <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> project built for the CS4421 DevOps module at
		the University of Limerick. The static pages are served from Amazon S3 through CloudFront, and the
		dynamic version runs as a Docker container on AWS with a <code>/api/health</code> probe. The colour
		keyboard uses the Web Audio API: every note is synthesised in your browser and lit with Scriabin's
		colour for its key.
	</p>
</Layout>
